course: dictionary
lesson: 8036
title: Refuse: saying no
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To refuse means to say no, or to not do something you are asked to do. You choose not to go along with it, and you do not change your mind.
explain: «David had the chance to kill King Saul, who was hunting him, but refused to harm him.» David could have hurt Saul, but he chose not to. Test your meaning: swap in «said no to» and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: You can also refuse something, which means not accepting it: «she refused the offer». The clue is offer, something someone holds out to you that you can take or leave.
explain: Refusing can keep you safe. A guide dog that «refuses» to walk forward when a car is coming is protecting the woman it guides. Saying no to danger is a brave and sensible choice.
fact: «Refuse» as a verb, said ri-FYOOZ, means to say no or to not accept something.
fact: The other forms are «refused» and «refusing»: she refused, and she is refusing.
fact: As a noun, said REF-yoos, «refuse» means rubbish or waste, as in «refuse collection», the rubbish collection.
fact: Refusing to go with a stranger, to keep an unsafe secret, or to join in bullying are all safe, strong choices.
exercise: In the story David «refused to harm» King Saul. What does refused mean here? | Gave him a gift | *Said no and would not hurt him | Went to hunt him down | Asked him to come home
exercise: The guide dog «refuses» to walk forward when a car is coming. Why is this a good refusal? | It means the dog is lost | *It keeps the woman safe | It makes the car go faster | It shows the dog is hungry
exercise: In «refuse collection», what does refuse mean? | Going to school | Saying no | *Rubbish or waste | Accepting a gift
test: She «refused the offer» of a lift home. What does refused mean here? | Lost it | *Did not accept it | Took it gladly | Gave it back to the driver
test: Which of these is a safe thing to refuse? | To help a friend with homework | To say thank you | *To go with a stranger who offers you sweets | To wash your hands
exam: Mia's friend asks her to keep an unsafe secret. What should Mia do, using refuse? | *Refuse to keep it, and tell a trusted adult | Spread the secret around the class | Keep it, because friends always share secrets | Hide the secret from everybody
